Merger Agreement:
Section 8.2 Superior Acquisition Evaluation. Notwithstanding any other provision in this Agreement, upon receipt of a proposed Acquisition Offer, the Company's Board shall evaluate whether the offer qualifies as a Superior Proposal. For this determination, the Board must: 
(i) Evaluate the financial terms of the proposal;
(ii) Consult with its legal advisors to ensure that the proposal complies with applicable regulatory standards and fiduciary duties;
(iii) Analyze the strategic impact of the offer on the Company’s long-term operational goals and competitiveness, as detailed in Section 5.1;
(iv) Enter into a mandatory negotiation period with Parent Company representatives to address any amendments, including those pertaining to operational and strategic factors;
(v) Fully disclose to shareholders both quantitative financial metrics and qualitative aspects such as innovation potential and market share implications.

